# Line endings are a test-result variable on this estate, not a preference. Every clone
# here has core.autocrlf=true, so without this file the working tree holds CRLF while CI
# holds LF, and a test that compares exact file content passes in one place and fails in
# the other. Pinning the working tree to LF makes the two agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts, named even though `*` already covers them: this is the case where a
# CRLF is a runtime failure rather than a noisy diff. A shebang ending in a carriage
# return makes a container report `bad interpreter`, and 40-inject-env.sh sat at
# w/crlf on a Windows clone while the repo held lf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows launchers must keep CRLF or cmd.exe cannot run them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Tracked binaries: never normalise, never diff.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
